      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 3,
      "comment": "Judge rationale contradicts itself (calls \"Seville\" an error, then says the tool also says Seville). Checked: Seville and Aix-en-Provence are grounded in the wiki_search result, as are the 1801-1810 territorial censuses. Only a small overstatement: one line calls the tax lists in 1927171 \"the primary name indexes\" while another line says the collection only \"may include\" them. Not a 2."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_locality_guide_007",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Correctness",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 3,
      "comment": "Judge error. I checked the guide text: it says the four wiki_place_page sections and the California wiki_read pages returned generic content — true, all served by the wiki-read-any / wiki-place-page-any catch-alls. It never says wiki_search was generic, and it actually cites the wiki_search Gold Rush result for Bancroft and the State Library. No factual error."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_locality_guide_v7h",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Correctness",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The guide does NOT print ulsterancestry.com — it prints ancestryireland.com, the correct domain. But the skill never called wiki_read on Ireland_Church_Records, so no tool in this run returned that URL; it came from memory. There is also a real error: it calls Ballylinny a \"neighboring civil parish\", while the tool result puts Ballylinny in Lower Belfast barony at the opposite end of the county from Bushmills, so \"the same pattern applies\" is misleading."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_locality_guide_v7h",
