      "comment": "The guide never mentions Ballylinny, so it did not adopt the volume place-label — the passing behaviour for the failure under test. But it has real errors: it says to pull First Bushmills Presbyterian from IrishGenealogy.ie (which holds no Antrim Presbyterian registers), calls Antrim town the county/assize town (assizes sat at Carrickfergus, later Belfast), and calls Ballymoney an assize town (it was not)."
